2. Reference screenshots (512 Pixels), not in this repository
-------------------------------------------------------------

The visual reference is the macOS 10.15 Catalina gallery of the 512 Pixels
Aqua Screenshot Library:

    https://512pixels.net/projects/aqua-screenshot-library/macos-10-15-catalina/

The 294 screenshots are third-party images. They are not in the repository:
reference/screenshots/ is listed in .gitignore. `npm run reference:fetch` downloads them from
512 Pixels to a developer's machine for local comparison and verifies each
against the hash in reference/manifest.json. The MIT licence grants no rights
in them.

Some demo data reproduces text that is visible in those screenshots, so that a
demo can be compared with its capture: for example one dictionary article
(demos/dictionary/dictionary-data.ts), the title and author of the one book in
the Books capture (demos/books/books-data.ts), and log lines in the Console
captures (demos/console/console-data.ts). The files say where they do this.


3. Apple
--------

Macalicious reproduces the appearance and behaviour of the macOS 10.15
Catalina interface, which is Apple's design. macOS, Catalina, Aqua, Finder,
Safari, the names of the other applications and San Francisco are trademarks
of Apple Inc. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Apple, and
the MIT licence grants no rights in Apple's designs or trademarks.

No file taken from macOS is in the repository: no Apple font, icon, desktop
picture, sound or system image. Controls are drawn in CSS, glyphs are redrawn
as CSS shapes or inline SVG, and text falls back to Inter where San Francisco
is not installed. Alert sounds are synthesised in the browser.


4. Generated artwork
--------------------

293 WebP images in the demos were produced with an image model
(gpt-image-2.5, added on 8 October 2026):

- demos/desktop/icons/ (56): icons for the applications, folders, documents,
  volumes and the Trash.
- demos/desktop/art/ (2) and
  demos/system-preferences/panes/desktop-and-screen-saver/art/ (26): desktop
  pictures and their thumbnails.
- demos/app-store/art/ (61), demos/photos/art/ (48), demos/news/art/ (34),
  demos/books/art/ (17), demos/safari/art/ (12), demos/tv/art/ (12),
  demos/music/art/ (8), demos/podcasts/art/ (8), demos/messages/art/ (5), and
  one each in demos/facetime/art/, demos/photo-booth/art/, demos/preview/art/
  and demos/quicktime-player/art/: covers, photographs, story pictures,
  invented application artwork and portraits of invented people.

These files are not Apple's, but the icons and several of the desktop pictures
were made to resemble Catalina's: the icons follow the subject, shape and
colour of the Catalina application icons closely, and some desktop pictures
carry the names of Apple's (catalina-day, mojave-day, solar-gradients-day).
The MIT licence is offered for whatever rights exist in the generated files
and cannot grant any right in the Apple designs they resemble.

The 12 WebP images in demos/help-viewer/pictures/ are captures of this
project's own desktop, taken by capture.mjs in the same folder; they show the
generated icons and desktop picture.


